 $-2,$ and\n\n- the open circle at $2$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $2.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x<-2$ or $x>2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-553a4e4d-d3cf-540f-985f-b11ce4faee73"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-553a4e4d-d3cf-540f-985f-b11ce4faee73" :answer-field/id #uuid "553a4e4d-d3cf-540f-985f-b11ce4faee73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fbb29ba7-4e18-5849-879e-c49a72bf9554" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5f59290c-f99e-50bf-8357-7481d3dec84c" "answer-fbb29ba7-4e18-5849-879e-c49a72bf9554" "answer-8717804d-3968-5df1-bef6-5084eb1e76f4" "answer-113fb996-f646-5f2c-a2c1-2ddf035922b9" "answer-bd4e7bef-debd-5f20-a074-e3872aadf2c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f59290c-f99e-50bf-8357-7481d3dec84c" :answer/id #uuid "5f59290c-f99e-50bf-8357-7481d3dec84c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x<-2$ or $x<2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbb29ba7-4e18-5849-879e-c49a72bf9554" :answer/id #uuid "fbb29ba7-4e18-5849-879e-c49a72bf9554" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x<-2$ or $x>2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8717804d-3968-5df1-bef6-5084eb1e76f4" :answer/id #uuid "8717804d-3968-5df1-bef6-5084eb1e76f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x>-2$ or $x<2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-113fb996-f646-5f2c-a2c1-2ddf035922b9" :answer/id #uuid "113fb996-f646-5f2c-a2c1-2ddf035922b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x\\le -2$ or $x\\ge 2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd4e7bef-debd-5f20-a074-e3872aadf2c3" :answer/id #uuid "bd4e7bef-debd-5f20-a074-e3872aadf2c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x\\le -2$ or $x\\le 2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-322d7cc1-ec63-5690-b8ff-cb69089ad748" :question/id #uuid "322d7cc1-ec63-5690-b8ff-cb69089ad748" :question/math-academy-id "q-181311" :question/problem "![](images/26/264828b133192b7fff74cfef0718ec56cf82d638003bb9774c2318cb3ae2cc2c.png)\n\nThe inequality corresponding to the highlighted region shown above is $x${{field-1}}\n$1\\text{ or }x$\n{{field-2}}$4.$" :question/worked-solution "The red rays contain all values less than $1$ or greater than $4.$ In addition, \n\n- the open circle at $1$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $1,$ and\n\n- the closed circle at $4$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $4.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x<1$ or $x\\ge 4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dda1edb5-23e2-5439-94a9-f3319997eb31" "answer-field-a31d8aac-4a83-54fc-810d-72ae86787156"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dda1edb5-23e2-5439-94a9-f3319997eb31" :answer-field/id #uuid "dda1edb5-23e2-5439-94a9-f3319997eb31" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2213c361-0498-5c03-9c21-011df8f6c91b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2213c361-0498-5c03-9c21-011df8f6c91b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2213c361-0498-5c03-9c21-011df8f6c91b" :answer/id #uuid "2213c361-0498-5c03-9c21-011df8f6c91b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a31d8aac-4a83-54fc-810d-72ae86787156" :answer-field/id #uuid "a31d8aac-4a83-54fc-810d-72ae86787156" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ae9a9300-b57b-5372-b60a-9cb5e5cfc19e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae9a9300-b57b-5372-b60a-9cb5e5cfc19e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae9a9300-b57b-5372-b60a-9cb5e5cfc19e" :answer/id #uuid "ae9a9300-b57b-5372-b60a-9cb5e5cfc19e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ge" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a3a4f7e6-baa5-55ec-a1d3-42158ee1abc0" :question/id #uuid "a3a4f7e6-baa5-55ec-a1d3-42158ee1abc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-54814" :question/problem "Which of the following number lines represents the inequality $-4\\le x\\le 0?$" :question/worked-solution "The inequality $-4\\le x\\le 0$ means that $x$ can take any value greater than or equal to $-4,$ and less than or equal to $0.$\n\nTo represent this on a number line, we draw a closed circle at $-4$ and another closed circle at $0.$ Then, we highlight the region between the points.\n\n![](images/e8/e884f5bcda9ad664f00a59c8bffcd72ce21472b2cb9127c26ad5cdbd42c73fc5.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e1bb8844-0873-5c25-848c-50ce7cae27a4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e1bb8844-0873-5c25-848c-50ce7cae27a4" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1bb8844-0873-5c25-848c-50ce7cae27a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-94267add-f71f-5686-b434-135b5f7b2234" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d22d087b-5216-5bf5-9b0d-81e8626615b6" "answer-f4865b3e-1ec6-5037-b44d-d3d8c0ff4be3" "answer-94267add-f71f-5686-b434-135b5f7b2234" "answer-57251f80-249e-5c20-8e89-c0f2da08ef60" "answer-1ffbefb9-b444-5dc0-9cde-2b9b8e723e45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d22d087b-5216-5bf5-9b0d-81e8626615b6" :answer/id #uuid "d22d087b-5216-5bf5-9b0d-81e8626615b6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/5e/5e4cac903a7334f2962cb42cfab051e674d19753b1a755d71388863ed510652f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4865b3e-1ec6-5037-b44d-d3d8c0ff4be3" :answer/id #uuid "f4865b3e-1ec6-5037-b44d-d3d8c0ff4be3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/e1/e1607303de3b565e596e8fbad4894a06f5524729edab615cc38d3ce17b689c67.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94267add-f71f-5686-b434-135b5f7b2234" :answer/id #uuid "94267add-f71f-5686-b434-135b5f7b2234" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/e8/e884f5bcda9ad664f00a59c8bffcd72ce21472b2cb9127c26ad5cdbd42c73fc5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57251f80-249e-5c20-8e89-c0f2da08ef60" :answer/id #uuid "57251f80-249e-5c20-8e89-c0f2da08ef60" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ec/eca66ef7af9071162e2ded563a7419857c98026c92e2190416503a1f49197ebd.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ffbefb9-b444-5dc0-9cde-2b9b8e723e45" :answer/id #uuid "1ffbefb9-b444-5dc0-9cde-2b9b8e723e45" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f6/f67a6123a1028f9ced155b4752d11b2c3b40b6b4c367e7edbdb795cff294409d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138765 :question/problem "How is the inequality $-2\\le x<2$ represented on a number line?" :question/worked-solution "The inequality $-2\\le x<2$ means that $x$ can take any value greater than or equal to $-2,$ and less than $2.$\n\nTo represent this on a number line, we draw a closed circle at $-2$ and an open circle at $2.$ Then, we highlight the region between the points.\n\n![](images/23/235e6d5bbe12a7372cd3466d877793417e5b055e6120b622f1ec52481f16bae1.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135543 :answer-field/correct 17592186135544 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-7acb590f-26ef-56eb-bc17-cd672b435fa9" :question/id #uuid "7acb590f-26ef-56eb-bc17-cd672b435fa9" :question/math-academy-id "q-54811" :question/problem "![](images/2a/2ac03455fb1b259e0f31719c613d9f7c3adb50b7d8e96667514abb7c513ed0e3.png)\n\nWhich inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?" :question/worked-solution "The red segment contains all values between  $-1$ and $4.$ In addition,\n\n- the closed circle at $-1$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $-1,$ while\n\n- the closed circle at $4$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $4.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents  $-1\\le x\\le 4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9209c1da-7a51-5b49-93d6-ed78aa06adc3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9209c1da-7a51-5b49-93d6-ed78aa06adc3" :answer-field/id #uuid "9209c1da-7a51-5b49-93d6-ed78aa06adc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6338b55b-e48b-5949-b4d5-24206f357d11" :answer-field/choices ["answer-885b3826-1efb-5a7d-9b94-65d6791601e1" "answer-b670a909-c2f8-5e96-8301-2086b25995f1" "answer-6338b55b-e48b-5949-b4d5-24206f357d11" "answer-1acf19ca-e1ca-52d2-a28d-44666d70c49b" "answer-5225eda9-90f4-5021-862a-16c2df28136c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-885b3826-1efb-5a7d-9b94-65d6791601e1" :answer/id #uuid "885b3826-1efb-5a7d-9b94-65d6791601e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1<x<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b670a909-c2f8-5e96-8301-2086b25995f1" :answer/id #uuid "b670a909-c2f8-5e96-8301-2086b25995f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1>x>4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6338b55b-e48b-5949-b4d5-24206f357d11" :answer/id #uuid "6338b55b-e48b-5949-b4d5-24206f357d11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\le x\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1acf19ca-e1ca-52d2-a28d-44666d70c49b" :answer/id #uuid "1acf19ca-e1ca-52d2-a28d-44666d70c49b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x<-1$ or  $x>4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5225eda9-90f4-5021-862a-16c2df28136c" :answer/id #uuid "5225eda9-90f4-5021-862a-16c2df28136c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x\\le -1$ or $x\\ge 4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4c6aaf3a-5087-5971-9f06-dcb66d6db1fe" :question/id #uuid "4c6aaf3a-5087-5971-9f06-dcb66d6db1fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-181351" :question/problem "![](images/94/945f83a6af821028b133995ddc13193b325ce9cea7d97c8617532369b570542e.png)\n\nThe inequality corresponding to the highlighted region shown above is $-1${{field-1}}\n$x$\n{{field-2}}$3.$" :question/worked-solution "The red segment contains all values between  $-1$ and $3.$ In addition,\n\n- the closed circle at $-1$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $-1,$ while\n\n- the closed circle at $3$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $3.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents  $-1\\le x\\le 3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b3ff8f56-6b9b-5142-b224-919447b3f5b3" "answer-field-a2e93860-dc13-5b93-b690-288897a1f382"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b3ff8f56-6b9b-5142-b224-919447b3f5b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3ff8f56-6b9b-5142-b224-919447b3f5b3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-cfae532f-c456-5e73-96f1-4e2ba80f59fc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cfae532f-c456-5e73-96f1-4e2ba80f59fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfae532f-c456-5e73-96f1-4e2ba80f59fc" :answer/id #uuid "cfae532f-c456-5e73-96f1-4e2ba80f59fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a2e93860-dc13-5b93-b690-288897a1f382" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2e93860-dc13-5b93-b690-288897a1f382" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-314de0d5-98a7-53fa-9fff-2bf5ecb570f5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-314de0d5-98a7-53fa-9fff-2bf5ecb570f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-314de0d5-98a7-53fa-9fff-2bf5ecb570f5" :answer/id #uuid "314de0d5-98a7-53fa-9fff-2bf5ecb570f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186139662 :tutorial/content "A **compound inequality** is an inequality that consists of multiple different inequalities put together. For example, the compound inequality \n\n$$\nx \\leq 0 \\hspace{.25cm} \\text{ or } \\hspace{.25cm} x \\gt  3\n$$\n\n states that $x$ is less than or equal to $0$, or greater than $3$.\n\nFor the compound \"or\" inequality to be satisfied, at least one of the separate inequalities must be satisfied. To illustrate:\n\n- $x=-1$ satisfies the inequality because it satisfies $x \\leq 0.$\n\n- $x=5$ satisfies the inequality because it satisfies $x > 3.$\n\n- $x=1$ does not satisfy the inequality because it does not satisfy $x \\leq 0$ and it also does not satisfy $x > 3.$\n\nTo graph a compound inequality involving the word \"or,\" we graph the two separate inequalities on the same number line. In this particular case,\n\n- the inequality $x \\leq 0$ consists of a closed circle at $0$ and an arrow to the left, while\n\n- the inequality $x >3$ consists of an open circle at $3$ and an arrow to the right.\n\nThe resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/96/96f1b1ee25ebc210a83ba12d90396683b7e2660050f820c4057ab85de419db91.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186139663 :tutorial/content "Compound inequalities can also be written with the word \"and.\" However, such inequalities are often written together as a single expression with two inequality signs. For example, the compound inequality \n\n$$\n-4 \\leq x < -1\n$$\n\n means that $-4 \\leq x$ and $x < -1.$\n\nFor the compound \"and\" inequality to be satisfied, both of the separate inequalities must be satisfied. To illustrate:\n\n- $x=-3$ satisfies the inequality because it satisfies both $-4 \\leq x$ and $x < -1.$\n\n- $x=-5$ does not satisfy the inequality because it does not satisfy $-4 \\leq x.$\n\n- $x=0$ does not satisfy the inequality because it does not satisfy $x < -1.$\n\nTo graph this compound inequality, we first graph the two inequalities separately.\n\n![](images/42/42edf8ee61badbbd1e5525a3843cfbe189e6432b2ad06455c1bdca6a7087ac56.png)\n\nThen, we keep only where they overlap.\n\n![](images/fa/fa07233f96bed30ddfcc5905a55a835763359cd34188e4d1c249c13b1d27d25c.png)\n\n**Note:** Any compound \"and\" inequality will always represent a segment between two points. So, it is not always necessary to draw both inequalities and find the overlap. To speed up the process, we can just draw the endpoints with open or closed circles as appropriate, and highlight the area between the endpoints." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138614 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
